# Plan Mode → docs/plans

When using **Plan Mode** (or when the user attaches a `.plan.md` from Cursor):

1. **After the plan is approved** (before or right after Build), copy it to `docs/plans/<kebab-case-name>.plan.md`.
   - Derive the filename from the plan `name` frontmatter (e.g. `Gene Feature Effect Size` → `gene-feature-effect-size.plan.md`).
   - Do **not** keep only `~/.cursor/plans/*_<hash>.plan.md` — that path is outside normal commits.

2. **Normalize frontmatter** to match existing plans in `docs/plans/`:
   - Keep `name`, `overview`, `todos` (with `id`, `content`, `status`).
   - Add a `> **Status: …**` line under `overview` when implementation starts or finishes.
   - Remove `isProject: false` (repo-local plans do not need it).
   - Add `azure_devops:` block as a **Feature** under Epic **AB#413** (MethylPipeline platform); see [`docs/plans/alignment-qc-screening.plan.md`](docs/plans/alignment-qc-screening.plan.md). Set `work_item_id` / per-todo `work_item_id` after creating Boards items (or re-run `scripts/ado_traceability/`).

3. **Update `docs/plans/README.md`** — add a row to the work-item mapping table when the plan is Feature-sized under AB#413.

4. **On merge / task completion** — set each finished todo to `status: completed` in the plan file in the same commit as the code when practical.

5. **Commit messages** — reference the plan file and todo / `AB#` id (see `docs/plans/README.md`).

Example promotion:

```
docs/plans/gene-feature-effect-size.plan.md
```

Reference in PR body: `Implements gene-feature-effect-size plan (biology-weight-matrix, …) (AB#467)`.
